1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,281
Search "Form Trigger" in your node panel and add "n8n Form." Unlike the IMAP node,

2
00:00:05,281 --> 00:00:08,649
this one opens a small menu first: Triggers and Actions.

3
00:00:08,649 --> 00:00:13,581
You want the trigger, "On new n8n Form event." Why is a manual paste not cheating,

4
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:15,325
in a course about automation?

5
00:00:15,325 --> 00:00:19,655
Because you should spend integration effort where the hours actually go.

6
00:00:19,655 --> 00:00:24,526
Priya's twenty minutes per call went on reading the transcript and distilling it,

7
00:00:24,526 --> 00:00:29,096
not on moving the file, and the agent removes the twenty minutes either way.

8
00:00:29,096 --> 00:00:34,088
Meanwhile every live connection you add is a credential to guard, a blast radius to

9
00:00:34,088 --> 00:00:38,117
think about, and a thing that breaks when the meeting tool updates.

10
00:00:38,117 --> 00:00:39,981
A form has none of those costs.

11
00:00:39,981 --> 00:00:44,311
The judgement, which is the entire value, is identical down both routes.

12
00:00:44,311 --> 00:00:45,995
Automate the thinking first.

13
00:00:45,995 --> 00:00:49,543
Automate the transport the day the transport is what hurts.

14
00:00:49,543 --> 00:00:54,595
Later, if you decide the paste step is one click too many, you can swap this trigger

15
00:00:54,595 --> 00:00:59,466
for a folder watcher on wherever your meeting tool saves transcripts, and nothing

16
00:00:59,466 --> 00:01:01,090
else in this build changes.

17
00:01:01,090 --> 00:01:05,661
That upgrade is worth knowing exists, even if you do not need it on day one.

18
00:01:06,211 --> 00:01:10,907
You now have a working intake for this agent, and you did not touch a single

19
00:01:10,907 --> 00:01:12,205
credential to get it.

20
00:01:12,205 --> 00:01:17,334
That is worth noticing: not every agent in this course needs the setup weight Agent

21
00:01:17,334 --> 00:01:17,705
1 did.

22
00:01:17,705 --> 00:01:22,711
Name the three fields with a little care, because these names are not labels on a

23
00:01:22,711 --> 00:01:27,716
page, they are the columns of the wire table the next lecture's prompt will point

24
00:01:27,716 --> 00:01:27,902
at.

25
00:01:27,902 --> 00:01:32,969
Meeting title, Attendees, Transcript: plain words you will recognise from the left

26
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:35,379
hand panel when you build the briefing.

27
00:01:35,379 --> 00:01:40,570
The attendees field earns its place in a specific way: the transcript says "Sam will

28
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:45,576
send the figures", and the agent can only turn that into a real owner if it knows

29
00:01:45,576 --> 00:01:47,183
which Sam was in the room.

30
00:01:47,183 --> 00:01:50,026
You are not filling in a form for bureaucracy.

31
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:55,217
You are handing the agent the context the transcript itself forgets to say out loud.

32
00:01:55,217 --> 00:02:00,160
Set the transcript field to the multi line type, save, and open the Test URL n8n

33
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:05,166
gives you, just to see your own intake page exist: a private little web page that

34
00:02:05,166 --> 00:02:07,020
did not exist two minutes ago.

35
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:09,646
Neither route is the "proper" one.

36
00:02:09,646 --> 00:02:14,409
The form is simply the one this course can teach without asking you to trust a

37
00:02:14,409 --> 00:02:15,997
screen it cannot show you.

38
00:02:15,997 --> 00:02:19,173
Pick whichever one you will actually use every week.

39
00:02:19,173 --> 00:02:24,302
One more honest word on the right hand card, because "export format" sounds abstract

40
00:02:24,302 --> 00:02:25,218
until it bites.

41
00:02:25,218 --> 00:02:30,165
Every meeting tool writes transcripts its own way: different file names, speakers

42
00:02:30,165 --> 00:02:32,546
marked differently, timestamps or none.

43
00:02:32,546 --> 00:02:37,554
A folder watcher inherits all of that, which means the day your workplace switches

44
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:42,256
meeting tools, the watcher route needs rebuilding and the form route does not

45
00:02:42,256 --> 00:02:42,684
notice.

46
00:02:42,684 --> 00:02:47,386
Text pasted into a box is the one format no vendor can change underneath you.

47
00:02:47,386 --> 00:02:52,332
The upgrade earns its keep at real volume, several transcribed calls a day, every

48
00:02:52,332 --> 00:02:52,576
day.

49
00:02:52,576 --> 00:02:57,584
Below that, the form's one click is cheaper than the watcher's maintenance, and it

50
00:02:57,584 --> 00:03:02,469
keeps a human glance in the loop at the exact moment the raw material enters the

51
00:03:02,469 --> 00:03:02,897
system.

52
00:03:03,447 --> 00:03:07,825
Worth pausing on the last box, because it is the honest heart of this build.

53
00:03:07,825 --> 00:03:10,763
The agent did not remove the work of meeting notes.

54
00:03:10,763 --> 00:03:15,430
It removed the transcription and drafting, and left the judgement: does this list

55
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:17,100
match the call I was just in?

56
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:21,882
That division of labour, machine drafts and human verifies, is the shape every good

57
00:03:21,882 --> 00:03:26,548
agent in this course settles into, and this diagram is the cleanest picture of it

58
00:03:26,548 --> 00:03:27,297
you will get.

59
00:03:27,847 --> 00:03:31,585
Before moving on, go and get a real transcript to build against.

60
00:03:31,585 --> 00:03:36,374
Most meeting tools have a transcription switch you may never have flipped; flip it

61
00:03:36,374 --> 00:03:41,280
on your next call, or export the text of a recent one if your tool keeps recordings.

62
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,448
No transcript handy?

63
00:03:42,448 --> 00:03:47,237
Spend three minutes narrating a fake weekly catch up to yourself with two or three

64
00:03:47,237 --> 00:03:50,157
commitments in it, names included, and paste that.

65
00:03:50,157 --> 00:03:54,829
What matters is that the next lecture's prompt gets built against text with real

66
00:03:54,829 --> 00:03:59,618
mess in it: half sentences, interruptions, a commitment made and then walked back.

67
00:03:59,618 --> 00:04:03,764
Clean sample text teaches the agent nothing about your actual Tuesdays.

68
00:04:03,764 --> 00:04:08,670
Next lecture is where this stops being an intake form and starts being an agent: the

69
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:12,641
prompt that reads a transcript and pulls the action items out of it.
